# Every combination of token kinds in positions 1, 2, 3 for toDt.
# Kinds: 1 digit, 2 digit <= 12, 2 digit 13-28, 2 digit > 31, month word, 4 digit.
# Each slot uses different values (5 6 7, 08 09 10, 14 15 16, 44 45 46, Sep Oct Nov, 2025 2026 2027)
# so that two readings can never coincide by accident.
# Separators are stripped before parsing, so a space stands in for '/', '-', etc.
# Rules: the orders y-m-d, m-d-y, d-m-y are all tried. A single valid distinct date is accepted.
# Several distinct valid dates is ambiguous and gives none, since no order has been established.
# 1 digit years are never valid. Out of range components give none rather than rolling over.
# The file runs as one evaluation. A failed parse never teaches an order and a unique reading is
# never affected by one, so all none results come first, followed by all the unique dates.

def show (str --)
    s!
    @s toDt match
        just d : $"{@s} -> {@d isoDateFmt}",
        none   : $"{@s} -> none",
    end wl
end

